\section{System Architecture}
The Suprakernel Sovereign Architecture is composed of five tightly integrated
layers: (i) the Sensor Ingestion Gate, (ii) the Riemannian Stress Manifold
Projection Layer, (iii) the Sovereign Execution Core, (iv) the Autonomous
Kernel Mutation Loop, and (v) the Telemetry and Stability Enforcement Layer.
Together, these components form a real-time autonomous kernel system capable of
self-modification under strict mathematical safety guarantees.

\subsection{Sensor Ingestion Gate}
The ingestion subsystem processes high-bandwidth data streams including
FITS/HDFS inputs, cluster telemetry, and state vectors $p(t)$. All incoming
signals are buffered through zero-copy, lock-free ring buffers to ensure
bounded latency and prevent memory fragmentation. The ingestion gate provides
the initial state for manifold projection and stability evaluation.

\subsection{Riemannian Stress Manifold Projection}
State vectors are mapped to the Riemannian stress manifold
$\mathcal{M}_{\text{stress}}$ via the $\Omega$-mapping operator:
\begin{equation}
\Omega : \mathbb{R}^n \rightarrow \mathcal{M}_{\text{stress}}.
\end{equation}
The manifold geometry encodes curvature, stress gradients, and deformation
fields relevant to stability. The Jacobian determinant $J(p)$ of the mapping is
monitored continuously to prevent manifold inversion or topological tearing.

\subsection{Sovereign Execution Core}
The sovereign core coordinates distributed GPU execution across a 64-node
NVIDIA HGX H100 cluster. Each node executes CUDA/PTX kernels synchronized via
NVLink 4.0 and RDMA-enabled MPI channels. The core manages:
\begin{itemize}
    \item distributed state updates,
    \item manifold-aware scheduling,
    \item resource allocation under stability constraints,
    \item real-time synchronization of Jacobian and Lyapunov metrics.
\end{itemize}
The execution core serves as the substrate on which autonomous kernel mutation
occurs.

\subsection{Autonomous Kernel Mutation Loop}
Runtime evolution is governed by the four-stage autodidact cycle:
\[
\text{Observe} \rightarrow \text{Orient} \rightarrow \text{Mutate} \rightarrow \text{Verify}.
\]

\paragraph{Observe.}
The system ingests $p(t)$ and telemetry $\mathcal{T}(t)$ through zero-copy
buffers, ensuring low-latency access to cluster-wide metrics.

\paragraph{Orient.}
The state is projected onto $\mathcal{M}_{\text{stress}}$, and the system
computes:
\begin{equation}
J(p), \qquad (\alpha - \beta), \qquad \nabla U(p),
\end{equation}
to assess geometric and dynamical stability.

\paragraph{Mutate.}
The JIT compiler proposes kernel updates $\Delta K$ subject to:
\begin{equation}
\|\Delta K\| \le \kappa_{\max}(t),
\end{equation}
where $\kappa_{\max}(t)$ is derived from real-time telemetry constraints.

\paragraph{Verify.}
Each mutation is accepted only if:
\begin{equation}
\dot{L}(p) < 0, \qquad
J(p) > 0, \qquad
\dot{h}(p) + \gamma_{\text{CBF}} h(p) \ge 0.
\end{equation}
This ensures that kernel evolution cannot destabilize the system.

\subsection{Telemetry and Stability Enforcement Layer}
A sovereign telemetry daemon streams:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{T}(t) = \{ J(p), \alpha(t), \beta(t), U(p),
B_{\text{mem}}, U_{\text{tensor}} \},
\end{equation}
into the execution core. These signals regulate:
\begin{itemize}
    \item adaptive damping $\mathbf{D}(p)$,
    \item mutation amplitude bounds $\kappa_{\max}(t)$,
    \item manifold curvature corrections,
    \item CBF enforcement via real-time quadratic programs.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Distributed Stability Coordination}
Across all nodes, the architecture maintains:
\begin{equation}
\dot{L}(p) < 0,\qquad
\langle \mathbf{D}(p), p \rangle \ge c_d \|p\|^2,\qquad
J(p) > 0.
\end{equation}
MPI/RDMA channels synchronize local manifold states, Lyapunov margins, mutation
decisions, and telemetry aggregates, ensuring global stability across the
cluster.

\subsection{Architectural Guarantees}
By construction, the architecture prohibits:
\begin{itemize}
    \item numerical divergence,
    \item manifold inversion,
    \item topological rupture,
    \item unstable kernel evolution.
\end{itemize}
All architectural components operate under mathematically certified stability
constraints.